Let's get both repositories initialized and structured cleanly through the terminal so your deployment pipeline stays locked down and modular.
### Step 1: awol-server Repository (Backend & Token-Gating Endpoints)
This repository will house your serverless functions, Guild API integration, Privy/Web3Auth verification, and session token generation.
#### 1. Directory Structure
```text
awol-server/
├── api/
│   └── verify-gated.js    # Endpoint for Guild role & session token verification
├── package.json
├── .env.example           # Template for environment variables (API keys, secrets)
└── README.md

```
#### 2. Terminal Initialization & Push Commands
Run these commands in your project root to initialize, secure, and push your server repo:
```bash
mkdir awol-server && cd awol-server
npm init -y
git init
echo "node_modules/\n.env" > .gitignore
git add .
git commit -m "feat: initialize awol-server architecture"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/awol-server.git
git push -u origin main

```
### Step 2: awol-contracts Repository (Smart Contracts)
This repository will hold your Solidity smart contracts, test suites, and deployment scripts for your token and gating logic.
#### 1. Directory Structure
```text
awol-contracts/
├── contracts/
│   └── AwolGate.sol       # Your smart contract logic
├── scripts/
│   └── deploy.js          # Deployment automation scripts
├── test/
│   └── AwolGate.test.js   # Test suite
├── hardhat.config.js      # Hardhat configuration
├── package.json
└── .env.example

```
#### 2. Terminal Initialization & Push Commands
Navigate out of your server folder and set up the contracts repository:
```bash
cd ..
mkdir awol-contracts && cd awol-contracts
npm init -y
git init
echo "node_modules/\ncache/\nartifacts/\n.env" > .gitignore
git add .
git commit -m "feat: initialize awol-contracts workspace"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/awol-contracts.git
git push -u origin main

```
Which repository would you like to drop the first functional code block into—the server endpoint logic or the smart contract?
